 1069 "q-132193" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424573 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424573 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that the random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}(\\sqrt{2}),$ calculate $P(X>\\sqrt{2}).$ Round your final answer to four decimal places." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424573 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "04d4be2b-e767-5839-99c5-470d8cac4dc9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424573 #edb/ref 1074 "An exponential random variable $X$ with rate $\\lambda $ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\lambda {e}^{-\\lambda x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that\n\n$$\nX∼\\text{Exp}(\\sqrt{2}).\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{2}{e}^{-\\sqrt{2}x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $P(X>\\sqrt{2})$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>\\sqrt{2}) & ={\\int }_{\\sqrt{2}}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\sqrt{2}}^{\\infty }\\sqrt{2}{e}^{-\\sqrt{2}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{-\\sqrt{2}x}{|}_{\\sqrt{2}}^{\\infty } \\\\  & ={e}^{-2} \\\\  & ≈0.1353\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424574 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186424566 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424574 #edb/ref 1069 "q-253935" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424574 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424574 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that the random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}(3),$ calculate $P(X\\le \\frac{5}{6}\\,|\\,X>\\frac{2}{3}).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424574 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "15d3a8f7-57e9-5955-b347-e7b15292f88f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424574 #edb/ref 1074 "Given a random variable $X∼Exp(\\lambda ),$ and two positive real numbers $s,t,$ the memoryless property of the exponential distribution states that\n\n$$\nP(X>s+t\\,|\\,X>s)=P(X>t)={e}^{-\\lambda t}.\n$$\n\nWe can compute the complementary conditional probability as follows:\n\n$$\nP(X\\le s+t\\,|\\,X>s)=1-P(X>s+t\\,|\\,X>s)=1-{e}^{-\\lambda t}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $\\lambda =3,$ $s=\\frac{2}{3},$ and $s+t=\\frac{5}{6}.$ From this, we can find $t$ as follows:\n\n$$\nt=(t+s)-s=\\frac{5}{6}-\\frac{2}{3}=\\frac{1}{6}\n$$\n\nSubstituting these values into the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le \\frac{5}{6}\\,|\\,X>\\frac{2}{3}) & =1-{e}^{-\\lambda t} \\\\  & =1-{e}^{-(3)\\cdot (1/6)} \\\\  & =1-{e}^{-1/2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424575 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186424567 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424575 #edb/ref 1069 "q-132173" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424575 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424575 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that the random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}(\\frac{1}{5}),$ calculate $P(X\\le 2).$ Round your final answer to four decimal places." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424575 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "377d9ecb-b1f2-5b7d-b293-34044d6f6558" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424575 #edb/ref 1074 "An exponential random variable $X$ with rate $\\lambda $ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\lambda {e}^{-\\lambda x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that\n\n$$\nX∼\\text{Exp}(\\frac{1}{5}).\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{5}{e}^{-x/5}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $P(X\\le 2)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 2) & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{5}{e}^{-x/5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{{e}^{-x/5}|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-2/5}+{e}^{0} \\\\  & ≈0.3297\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424576 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186424565 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424576 #edb/ref 1069 "q-132179" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424576 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424576 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that the random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}(\\sqrt{3}),$ calculate $P(X<\\frac{1}{3}).$ Round your final answer to four decimal places." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424576 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4b3ef3ac-d2db-5eb8-8c5f-a033b26be69b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424576 #edb/ref 1074 "An exponential random variable $X$ with rate $\\lambda $ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\lambda {e}^{-\\lambda x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that\n\n$$\nX∼\\text{Exp}(\\sqrt{3}).\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3}{e}^{-\\sqrt{3}x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $P(X<\\frac{1}{3})$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<\\frac{1}{3}) & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/3}\\sqrt{3}{e}^{-\\sqrt{3}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{-\\sqrt{3}x}{|}_{0}^{1/3} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-\\sqrt{3}/3}+{e}^{0} \\\\  & ≈0.4386\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424577 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186424572 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424577 #edb/ref 1069 "q-96347" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424577 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424577 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that the random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}(\\frac{1}{3}),$ calculate $P(2<X<3).$ Round your final answer to four decimal places." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424577 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9bd8d602-6713-5d8a-8e29-384c77e10125" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424577 #edb/ref 1074 "An exponential random variable $X$ with rate $\\lambda $ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\lambda {e}^{-\\lambda x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that\n\n$$\nX∼\\text{Exp}(\\frac{1}{3}).\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{-x/3}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $P(2<X<3)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(2<X<3) & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{-x/3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{-x/3}{|}_{2}^{3} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-1}+{e}^{-2/3} \\\\  & ≈0.1455\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424578 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186424569 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424578 #edb/ref 1069 "q-253936" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424578 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424578 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that the random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}(\\frac{3}{5}),$ calculate $P(X\\le 9\\,|\\,X>4).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424578 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a86905dc-6d69-50e5-afb3-4d8bb353dbfd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424578 #edb/ref 1074 "Given a random variable $X∼Exp(\\lambda ),$ and two positive real numbers $s,t,$ the memoryless property of the exponential distribution states that\n\n$$\nP(X>s+t\\,|\\,X>s)=P(X>t)={e}^{-\\lambda t}.\n$$\n\nWe can compute the complementary conditional probability as follows:\n\n$$\nP(X\\le s+t\\,|\\,X>s)=1-P(X>s+t\\,|\\,X>s)=1-{e}^{-\\lambda t}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $\\lambda =\\frac{3}{5},$ $s=4,$ and $s+t=9.$ From this, we can find $t$ as follows:\n\n$$\nt=(t+s)-s=9-4=5\n$$\n\nSubstituting these values into the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 9\\,|\\,X>4) & =1-{e}^{-\\lambda t} \\\\  & =1-{e}^{-(3/5)\\cdot (5)} \\\\  & =1-{e}^{-3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424579 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186424570 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424579 #edb/ref 1069 "q-96412" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424579 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424579 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that the random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}(8),$ calculate $P(X>0.4).$ Round your final answer to four decimal places." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424579 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "be9c7f67-1bb2-5f32-8555-0a5418fba86d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424579 #edb/ref 1074 "An exponential random variable $X$ with rate $\\lambda $ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\lambda {e}^{-\\lambda x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that\n\n$$\nX∼\\text{Exp}(8).\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}8{e}^{-8x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $P(X>0.4)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>0.4) & ={\\int }_{0.4}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0.4}^{\\infty }8{e}^{-8x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{-8x}{|}_{0.4}^{\\infty } \\\\  & ={e}^{-3.2} \\\\  & ≈0.0408\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424580 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186424571 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424580 #edb/ref 1069 "q-96421" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424580 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424580 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that the random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}(1),$ calculate $P(0.5\\le X\\le 2).$ Round your final answer to four decimal places." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424580 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d71bf438-c740-5ac5-956a-edf3ba9d43d6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424580 #edb/ref 1074 "An exponential random variable $X$ with rate $\\lambda $ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\lambda {e}^{-\\lambda x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that\n\n$$\nX∼\\text{Exp}(1).\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $P(0.5\\le X\\le 2)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0.5\\le X\\le 2) & ={\\int }_{0.5}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0.5}^{2}{e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{-x}{|}_{0.5}^{2} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-2}+{e}^{-0.5} \\\\  & ≈0.4712\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
